pcbkit 1

// RP2350A (Raspberry Pi): RP2350A dual Arm Cortex-M33 / Hazard3 RISC-V MCU, 150 MHz, 520 KB SRAM,
// external QSPI flash, USB 1.1 device/host, 3 PIO blocks (12 state machines), HSTX, 4 ADC inputs,
// 30 GPIO, internal 1.1 V switching regulator, QFN-60 7 x 7 mm (the Raspberry Pi Pico 2's chip)
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/RP2350A.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet: https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/rp2350/rp2350-datasheet.pdf (RP2350 datasheet
// build 06a7f75e58a1; Hardware design with RP2350 build 06a7f75e58a1 (2026-08-20))
// Pins: Raspberry Pi RP2350 datasheet (build 06a7f75e58a1): figure 152 QFN-60 pinout (label
// positions read from the PDF), 1.2.2 pin descriptions, table 3 GPIO functions, 14.1 QFN-60
// package dimensions, 14.9.5 table 1688 power supplies; Hardware design with RP2350 (same build):
// regulator, decoupling, crystal, flash and USB components
// Footprint: computed per IPC-7351B from the datasheet's package dimensions
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: As on the Raspberry Pi Pico 2: GPIO25 drives the LED, GPIO26-GPIO29 are the four ADC
// inputs, the USB bootloader expects a 12 MHz crystal.
// Note: All GPIOs are on IOVDD; they are 5 V tolerant while powered and 3.3 V failsafe unpowered,
// except as analog inputs.
// Note: The exposed pad (pin 61) is the only ground of the die: solder it with vias to the ground
// plane.
// Note: Runs firmware in PCBKit's RP2350 model (RISC-V cores): flash images with an IMAGE_DEF,
// flashed as a UF2 (family rp2350_riscv) onto the BOOTSEL drive; build with the rp2350 kit and
// name the program folder with `firmware` on the component. The memories are the board's: give
// the behavior's parameters flash_mib (the QSPI flash on chip select 0), and psram_mib and
// psram_cs (0, 8 or 19) for a PSRAM on QMI chip select 1.

/// RP2350A — RP2350A dual Arm Cortex-M33 / Hazard3 RISC-V MCU, 150 MHz, 520 KB SRAM, external
